  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Formation of photochemical smog involves the following reaction in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> are respectively.</p><p>(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>hu</mi></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></p><p>(ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p><p>(iii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>NO</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When fossil fuels are burnt, a variety of pollutants are emitted into the earth&rsquo;s&nbsp;troposphere.&nbsp;When these pollutants build up to sufficiently high levels, a chain reaction occurs from their interaction with sunlight in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi></math> is converted into nitrogen dioxide (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>). This&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in turn absorbs energy from sunlight and breaks up into nitric oxide and free oxygen atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>hv</mi></mover></mtd><mtd><mi>NO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Oxygen atoms are very reactive and combine with the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in air to produce ozone.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8652;</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The ozone formed in the above reaction (ii) reacts rapidly with the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> formed in reaction (i) to regenerate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> . <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is a brown gas and at sufficiently high levels can contribute to haze.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>NO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8594;</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iii</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>So, the A, B and C are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p>"
  }
}